From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:50:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] physim: noise declared by its intensity in world units
 (LabWorld.noise_intensity)

A field listed in noise_intensity reads its sd as the intensity of the
continuum noise: white draws are scaled by 1/dx (0.5/dx^2 for the conserved
flux divergence) and, with an ell in noise_corr, smoothed by the Gaussian at
unit gain for k = 0 instead of being rescaled to the white per-point variance.
The low-wavenumber spectrum is then sd^2 per native time whatever ell or dx;
the per-point sd falls like 1/(2 sqrt(pi) ell). At dx = 1 without ell it is
the white form bit for bit.

The per-step noise moves into LabStepper.add_noise unchanged. Existing
declarations are bit-identical to 77a6d83 (white in all three forms,
variance-matched noise_corr, runner_demo and vortex_demo declarations, signed
roster: sample bytes, generator state, declaration(); labeval's frozen suite
declarations unchanged).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
